#   /dev/ttyAMA0 -> mavlink-router  (TCP server 5760, UDP out 127.0.0.1:14550)
#   /dev/ttyAMA4 -> MicroXRCEAgent  (uXRCE-DDS; /usr/local/bin/MicroXRCEAgent serial -b 921600)
#   THESE ARE DIFFERENT WIRES. One can be dead while the other is healthy, so NAME WHICH LINK YOU
#     MEAN. "The FC is down" is not a diagnosis.
#   PX4 PARAMETERS ARE NOT EXPOSED OVER DDS AT ALL. tools/set_param.py must go via MAVLink on
#     ttyAMA0. CONSEQUENCE: if mavlink-router or AMA0 is down there is NO ROUTE TO ANY PARAM, even
#     with DDS perfectly healthy. Confirmed 10/10: "NO HEARTBEAT - MAVLink link down".
#   Conversely vehicle_status_v1, esc_status and the rest of the bridged set arrive over DDS on
#     AMA4, so ESC telemetry survives a MAVLink outage and vice versa.
#   TRAP, STILL PRESENT IN THE CONFIG: the mavlink-router stanza is NAMED
#     "[UartEndpoint serial-AMA4]" but its Device is /dev/ttyAMA0. THE STANZA NAME IS WRONG - AMA4
#     is the DDS port. Do not pick your wire from that label.
#   DDS fine but MAVLink dead still means THE FC IS ALIVE - reboot it over DDS.

