#--- RULER TRAPS THAT COST REAL TIME THIS PERIOD (all companion-side) ---
# THE ros2 CLI IS ITSELF AN UNRELIABLE RULER. node list ghosts for minutes after a stop; topic echo
#   and topic hz can return NOTHING on a provably live topic, --no-daemon included. Prove a node
#   dead with pgrep; measure with a direct rclpy subscriber. When the CLI goes quiet, reach for
#   MAVLink - never read the silence as the thing being dead.
# IT IS /fmu/out/vehicle_status_v1, NOT /fmu/out/vehicle_status. The unversioned name yields SILENCE
#   rather than an error, and a None default then reads as "disarmed" while the wheels are spinning.
#   PX4 message versioning is in effect across the bridged set, and that set is THIN and appears
#   LAZILY - check ros2 topic list before planning any measurement around a topic.
# BOOT-CLOCK TRAP: CHECK /proc/uptime BEFORE READING ANY DURATION OFF A TIMESTAMP. This box
#   restamps early boot and once forged a convincing "service up 11 hours" on a 4-minute-old unit.
#   A GAP in a timestamped log is not a fault either - grep timesyncd for a clock STEP first.
# NEVER READ A QUIET TOPIC AS EVIDENCE - prove a non-zero baseline first. Same for any detector:
#   prove the detector itself was live across the window.
# /scan DOES NOT TRACK BEYOND ~3 m - park about 2.5 m out. It also does not come back on its own
#   after a scan-killing test.
# NO RATE OR CPU NUMBER IS TRUSTWORTHY WITHOUT ps -eo pid,pcpu --sort=-pcpu FIRST - the rate you
#   measure may be reporting CPU starvation rather than the thing you meant to measure. Spikes
#   vanish before ps can see them; use ros2_ws/tools/cpu_catcher.sh.
# START A PERCEPTION MEASUREMENT, THEN GO QUIET. Commanding throughout starved the camera on 09/08
#   and produced two wrong answers.
# IS THE BOX ALIVE? tail -2 /var/log/ext5v/ext5v.csv - stamped every 2 s, independent of tmux and of
#   Claude, so a fresh row means ALIVE. Use it before ever cutting power on a silent terminal.
# ONE mavlink_shell.py PER FC BOOT (16/08). Retrying an empty result exhausts the sessions and KILLS
#   THE GCS MAVLINK LINK. Recovery is a reboot over DDS.
# Replays need ROS_DOMAIN_ID=42; the LIVE stack is domain 0.

